message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The Gregory-Laflamme threshold to order 1/n^12 and its resummation to AdS screening masses"
authors:
  - name: "Moki & Julio"
date-released: 2026-11-04
version: "1.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23940227"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hashirama1337s/large-d-gregory-laflamme"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - Gregory-Laflamme instability
  - large D
  - multiple zeta values
  - AdS/Ricci-flat correspondence
  - screening mass
  - Pade resummation
  - black holes
  - general relativity
  - large-D expansion
abstract: >-
  A black string is a black hole stretched along an extra dimension. If it is long enough, it is unstable and
  starts to break up.
  Exact large-dimension series of the black-string Gregory-Laflamme threshold to order 1/n^12 (multiple zeta values
  including zeta(5,3) and zeta(3,5,3)), a large-order law for its divergence, and its resummation, continued to n = -d,
  to the static screening masses of the AdS black brane. Data, code and sealed-test records included.
